 "unclear": [
  {
   "id": "U1",
   "text": "Parts pairing: whether a software lock that needs the maker's authorization is itself the lock section 5(c) forbids, or is lawful if the owner or a repairer can pair a genuine part with a tool the maker supplies on fair and reasonable terms.",
   "readings": [
    "U1-a: pairing that needs the maker's authorization is itself the forbidden lock; any part, genuine, salvaged or non-genuine, must work fully without contacting the maker, and makers must remove pairing from covered devices and leave it out of new ones",
    "U1-b: pairing continues; a lock is lawful if the owner or a repairer acting for the owner can pair a genuine part with a tool the maker supplies on fair and reasonable terms; makers may refuse to pair parts reported stolen and need not pair non-genuine parts"
   ],
   "components": {
